We may want to "merge" all remaining events from both `taskCh` and `pauseCh`, so I think we'd better return once both `taskCh` and `pauseCh` are closed.
Tips: a `nil` channel in go will block forever, so you may consume all data in the two channels via replacing the `!ok` branch with:
```go
// ...
if !ok {
  taskCh = nil
}
// ...
```
